steps.llm_prompt:
Create the initial GitHub AI Radar Canvas page.

RUN:
- Date: ${run_date}
- Time: ${run_time}
- Search query: ${radar_query}
- YouTube query: ${youtube_query}
- Stash space: ${space_id}

YOUTUBE SEARCH RESULTS:
- Result count: ${youtube_results_count}
- Top URL: ${youtube_top_url}
- Top results: ${youtube_top_results}

WEB SEARCH RESULTS:
${search_results.data}

BRAVE LLM CONTEXT:
- Grounding: ${brave_grounding}
- Sources: ${brave_sources}

VALIDATED CRAWLED SOURCES:
${validated_articles}

Output raw Markdown only. Do not output HTML. Do not output <!DOCTYPE>, <html>, <head>, <body>, <pre>, or any other wrapper tags. Do not wrap the answer in ```markdown, ```html, or any code fence. Use actual values and complete URLs; do not output curly-brace variable placeholders and do not shorten links.

Required structure:
# GitHub AI Radar

A one-paragraph purpose statement for this durable page.

## Latest Snapshot - ${run_date}
A concise summary of today's strongest signals.

## Featured Video
If Top URL is a real YouTube URL, include the video title/channel/published date when available, then put exactly one YouTube watch URL on its own line so Canvas can embed it. Do not include any other YouTube watch URLs elsewhere in the page. If Top URL is none, omit this section entirely.

## Notable Projects
A markdown table with columns: Project, Why it matters, Evidence, Source. Include 5-8 rows if evidence supports them. Project names should be repository or project names when available. Source must be a complete markdown link.

## Signals To Watch
Bullets for trends, repeated themes, or suspicious hype that needs verification.

## Sources
List every non-YouTube source URL used as a complete markdown link. Include the current featured YouTube URL only in the Featured Video section.

## Run Log
- ${run_date} ${run_time}: Initial radar page created from web search, Brave LLM Context, YouTube search when available, and validated crawled sources. Stash: ${space_id}

Refresh the existing GitHub AI Radar Canvas page by producing the full replacement Markdown content. Do NOT output only a delta, patch, summary, or new section. Preserve useful prior context from the existing page, but make the page current and easy to scan with today's snapshot first.

EXISTING PAGE CONTEXT TO PRESERVE COMPACTLY:
${radar_existing_content}

