- Sources: ${brave_sources}

VALIDATED CRAWLED SOURCES:
${validated_articles}

Output raw Markdown only. Do not output HTML. Do not output <!DOCTYPE>, <html>, <head>, <body>, <pre>, or any other wrapper tags. Do not wrap the answer in ```markdown, ```html, or any code fence. Use actual values and complete URLs; do not output curly-brace variable placeholders and do not shorten links.

Required full-page structure:
# GitHub AI Radar

A one-paragraph purpose statement for this durable page.

## Latest Snapshot - ${run_date}
A concise summary of today's strongest signals and what changed since the retained previous snapshots.

## Featured Video
If Top URL is a real YouTube URL, include the video title/channel/published date when available, then put exactly one YouTube watch URL on its own line so Canvas can embed the current feature. Do not include previous YouTube watch URLs anywhere else in the replacement page; summarize older videos as title text only if useful. If Top URL is none, omit this section entirely.

## Notable Projects
A markdown table with columns: Project, Why it matters, Evidence, Source. Include 5-8 rows if evidence supports them. Project names should be repository or project names when available. Source must be a complete markdown link.

## Signals To Watch
Bullets for trends, repeated themes, or suspicious hype that needs verification.

## Sources
List every non-YouTube source URL used as a complete markdown link. Include the current featured YouTube URL only in the Featured Video section.

## Previous Snapshots
Keep up to 7 brief dated bullets from the existing page context, newest first, and do not duplicate today's snapshot.

## Run Log
Keep up to 10 latest run-log entries, newest first.
- ${run_date} ${run_time}: Refreshed radar page with web search, Brave LLM Context, YouTube search when available, and validated crawled sources. Stash: ${space_id}
